userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add reusable error classification and an injected project-existence verdict helper.

**Motivation** — Nothing ever asks whether the project exists.

**Approach** — Apply these Design requirements verbatim:
- New `apps/web/lib/not-found.ts`: `isNotFoundError(err: unknown): boolean`, importing `ApiError` and `extractErrorStatus` from `~/composables/useApi`. It is true when `err` is an `ApiError` whose `code` is `404` or `40004`, or when `extractErrorStatus(err)` is `404`. It is false otherwise.
- New `apps/web/lib/project-route-check.ts`:

```ts
import { isNotFoundError } from '~/lib/not-found'

export type ProjectRouteVerdict = 'skip' | 'known' | 'found' | 'notFound' | 'unverified'

export interface ProjectRouteDeps {
  /** Slugs this tab already proved exist. */
  known: readonly string[]
  fetchProject: (slug: string) => Promise<unknown>
}

export async function checkProjectRoute(slug: unknown, deps: ProjectRouteDeps): Promise<ProjectRouteVerdict> {
  if (typeof slug !== 'string' || slug === '') return 'skip'
  if (deps.known.includes(slug)) return 'known'
  try {
    await deps.fetchProject(slug)
    return 'found'
  } catch (err) {
    return isNotFoundError(err) ? 'notFound' : 'unverified'
  }
}
```

Read-only integrations: `ApiError` in `apps/web/composables/useApi.ts`: `code: number`, thrown by `$api` for every enveloped failure. A missing project or ticket arrives as `code` `40004` (`NotFoundAppException`). Precedents: `isNotFound` in `pages/[project]/flows/[id].vue` and `pages/[project]/fleet/schedules/[id].vue` accept `404` or `40004`. `extractErrorStatus(err): number | undefined` in the same file: the HTTP status of a FetchError without an envelope.

**Scope** — In: these two pure modules and their unit tests. Out: wiring middleware/cache/navigation (US-003), ticket page state (US-004), title/error-page UI (US-005), palette/API changes (US-001/US-006/US-007), changing existing flows/schedules.

**Interface** — `isNotFoundError(err: unknown): boolean`; `ProjectRouteVerdict`, `ProjectRouteDeps` and `checkProjectRoute(slug: unknown, deps: ProjectRouteDeps): Promise<ProjectRouteVerdict>` exactly as above.

**Test implementation** — Create `tests/lib/not-found.spec.ts` for AC-1 to AC-4 and `tests/lib/project-route-check.spec.ts` for AC-5 to AC-10. Use the real ApiError export and injected fetchProject spies. No DB or network is necessary. Keep known-cache ownership out of the helper; only the later middleware appends successful slugs.

**Goal** — Check authenticated project routes before page mount and cache only successfully verified slugs.

**Motivation** — On that page the live-update stream keeps reopening against a 404 (F30).

**Approach** — Apply this Design verbatim:
- New `apps/web/middleware/project.global.ts`. It sorts after `auth.global.ts`, so it runs second:

```ts
import { apiPath } from '~/lib/api-path'
import { checkProjectRoute } from '~/lib/project-route-check'

export default defineNuxtRouteMiddleware(async (to) => {
  if (!useAuth().isAuthenticated.value) return
  const known = useState<string[]>('koda-known-projects', () => [])
  const { $api } = useApi()
  const slug = to.params.project
  const verdict = await checkProjectRoute(slug, { known: known.value, fetchProject: s => $api.get(apiPath`/projects/${s}`) })
  if (verdict === 'found' && typeof slug === 'string') known.value = [...known.value, slug]
  if (verdict === 'notFound') {
    return abortNavigation(createError({ statusCode: 404, statusMessage: 'Not Found', fatal: true }))
  }
})
```

`useState` carries the verified slugs from SSR into hydration, so a project is checked at most once per tab. A `'unverified'` verdict (a 403, an outage) is not cached, and navigation continues to the page's own states.

Failure Handling: The project check gets a failure that is not a 404 (403, 5xx, network): the verdict is `'unverified'`, navigation continues, the slug is not cached, and the page shows its own loading and error states, as today.

Read-only integrations: `apiPath` (tagged template) in `apps/web/lib/api-path.ts`: encodes each interpolated segment. `useAuth().isAuthenticated: ComputedRef<boolean>`. `middleware/auth.global.ts` runs first (global middleware run in file-name order), so it has already hydrated the session or redirected. `GET /api/projects/:slug` (`ProjectsController.findBySlug`): `200` with the project, `404` (`40004`) for an unknown or soft-deleted slug, and `403` for a non-member.

Extend the mount harness so that a route middleware can be loaded, and so that every component calling `useHead` mounts without a test-supplied stub. Another merged feature (`e2e-1121-ticket-page`) already edited the same `mount-sfc.ts` lists; keep this edit additive. In `apps/web/tests/helpers/mount-sfc.ts`, add `defineNuxtRouteMiddleware`, `abortNavigation` and `createError` to `NUXT_AUTO_IMPORTS`, so that the middleware spec can supply them through `globals`. Also add `useHead: () => undefined` to `AUTO_IMPORT_DEFAULTS`, so that every existing mount of a component that later calls `useHead` (`PageHeader`, `AppErrorPage`, the ticket page) still runs. A spec that tests a title overrides it through `globals`. Preserve all existing auto-import entries, including useNuxtData.

**Scope** — In: global middleware, additive shared harness support and real-middleware unit tests. Out: helper implementations (US-002), ticket state (US-004), 404-page presentation/titles (US-005), palette/API work, modifications to auth.global.ts. A project route answered with 403 (the viewer is not a member) keeps today's page error states: only a 404 becomes the not-found page. The verified-slug cache is never invalidated within a tab. A project deleted or renamed while the tab is open falls back to the page's own error states and the stream's existing capped retry. The live-update stream's handling of a 404 is unchanged: an `EventSource` cannot read the status, and the fix is that a missing project's page never mounts. Clearing the verified-slug cache (`koda-known-projects`) on logout or on a sign-in as another user in the same tab: it only skips a repeat existence check, and the page's own states still apply. Do not redesign the layout to hide a mounted unknown project; prevent mount instead.

**Interface** — Use the exact middleware above and US-002's `checkProjectRoute(slug: unknown, deps: ProjectRouteDeps): Promise<ProjectRouteVerdict>`. The cache key is exactly `koda-known-projects`.

**Test implementation** — Every AC loads the real `middleware/project.global.ts` through `loadSfc`, with `defineNuxtRouteMiddleware: fn => fn`, `createError: input => input`, a recording `abortNavigation`, authenticated useAuth by default, one shared `ref([])` for useState per test, and `useApi` returning `$api.get`. Pass `alias: { '~/composables/useApi': apiModule }` with the real ApiError module so instanceof uses the same class. Invoke the loaded default export with the route objects in the criteria. Create `tests/middleware/project-global.spec.ts`. Treat this as an authenticated navigation boundary: strict three-session TDD applies.
